Subject: [PATCH] modular: handle empty inputs in squeeze steps

The squeeze steps unwrapped the first output buffer, and their one-column and
one-row shortcuts read the rows of the average input up to the size of the
output. A horizontal squeeze without residual columns whose output tile is 1x1
but whose average input tile is empty (0x0) then panicked (image/internal.rs:
assertion failed: row < self.num_rows). Skip empty inputs and copy only what
the average input has. Test: test_fuzzer_squeeze_empty_inputs.

